        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: शोक",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "शोक — śok — \"mourning; grief\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दादा की मौत पर पूरे गाँव ने शोक मनाया। dādā kī maut par pūre gā̃v ne śok manāyā. The whole village mourned my grandfather's death."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "शोक (śok) is a tatsama, borrowed from Sanskrit śoka, \"sorrow, anguish, grief\" (Monier-Williams). śok manānā is to observe mourning."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
