          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दफ़नाना — dafnānā — \"to bury (the dead)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चिड़िया मर गई, तो बच्चों ने उसे बाग़ में दफ़नाया। ciṛiyā mar gaī, to baccoṁ ne use bāġ meṁ dafnāyā. The bird died, so the children buried it in the garden."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with ने (he or she …): उसने चिड़िया को दफ़नाया, usne ciṛiyā ko dafnāyā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दफ़नाना (dafnānā) is dafn, \"burial\", made into a verb with -ānā; dafn is usually traced to Arabic dafn, \"burial\", which reached Hindi through Persian."
            }
          ]
        },
